  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "To want, I would like to, to specify that",
   "texto": [
    "With a main verb in the present, we use the present conjunctive do: **Quero que venhas** (I want you to come), **Preciso que compres o pão** (I need you to buy the bread). With **gostaria**, it is natural the conjunctive peremptory: **Gostaria que me ajudasses** (I would like you to help me).",
    "Here it is enough to recognize this frequent form; its complete conjugation is studied below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Same subject: infinitive",
   "texto": [
    "If the subject is the same, use the infinitive and not the conjunctive: **Quero ir à praia** (I want to go to the beach), not **Quero que vou**. If the subject is another, use **que** + conjunctive: **Quero que tu vás** (I want you to go)."
   ]
  },
